{"tool_name":"bcbiornaseq","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"bcbiornaseq","home":"http://bioinformatics.sph.harvard.edu/bcbioRNASeq/","license":"MIT","summary":"Automated and scalable RNA-seq methods for identifying gene abundance counts.","addition_date":"2018-08-10T10:50:29Z","last_update_date":"2018-12-10T12:59:01Z","tool_type":["Library"],"version":["0.2.5"],"collections":["BioConductor"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:bcbiornaseq","credit":[{"email":"mike@steinbaugh.com","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://bioinformatics.sph.harvard.edu/bcbioRNASeq/reference/index.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"RNA-seq read count analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3563"}]}],"name":"bcbioRNASeq","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"aotamendi.1","publication":[{"doi":"10.12688/f1000research.12093.2","metadata":{"abstract":": \u00a9 2018 Steinbaugh MJ et al.RNA-seq analysis involves multiple steps, from processing raw sequencing data to identifying, organizing, annotating, and reporting differentially expressed genes. bcbio is an open source, community-maintained framework providing automated and scalable RNA-seq methods for identifying gene abundance counts. We have developed bcbioRNASeq, a Bioconductor package that provides ready-to-render templates, objects and wrapper functions to post-process bcbio RNA sequencing output data. bcbioRNASeq helps automate the generation of high-level RNA-seq reports, facilitating the quality control analyses, identification of differentially expressed genes and functional enrichment analyses.","authors":[{"name":"Barrera V."},{"name":"Chapman B.A."},{"name":"Hofmann O."},{"name":"Hutchinson J.N."},{"name":"Khetani R.S."},{"name":"Kirchner R.D."},{"name":"Mistry M."},{"name":"Pantano L."},{"name":"Piper M.E."},{"name":"Rutherford K.D."},{"name":"Steinbaug